# What Cloudflare Workers uploads/serves as static assets — separate from
# .gitignore, which only controls what git tracks. wrangler.jsonc's assets
# directory is "./" (the whole project root), so without this file EVERYTHING
# here — including .git internals and node_modules — is publicly fetchable
# at the live URL. Confirmed and fixed 2026-07-16 after .git/config turned
# out to be genuinely reachable at the deployed site.
.git/
.gitignore
.assetsignore
node_modules/
node_modules/**
node_modules/.*
package.json
package-lock.json
README.md
wrangler.jsonc
scripts/
# Added 2026-07-20 when the site moved from static-only to a real Worker
# script (src/index.js, for the anonymous usage-ping endpoints) — without
# these, the Worker's own source code and build temp files get uploaded
# and served as PUBLIC static files, exactly the same leak class as the
# .git incident above. Confirmed live: /src/index.js was reachable before
# this fix.
src/
.wrangler/
# Added 2026-08-11 alongside .claude/launch.json (the local `wrangler dev`
# preview config). Same leak class again — editor/tooling config is not site
# content and must never be served. Anything new at the top level that isn't
# a public page belongs here BEFORE the next deploy, not after.
.claude/
